## Grading rubric

The project is marked out of 100, plus up to 5 bonus points for the optional extension. Rigor and reasoning carry more weight than raw performance.

| Criterion | Weight | Excellent (full marks) | Weak |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Project difficulty | 10% | Challenging question (session transfer, cross-subject, executed-to-imagined transfer, confound analysis) carried through to a conclusion | Repeats a notebook exercise on the notebook’s data |
| Problem significance | 10% | Question matters for BCI use and is well grounded in 2–3 cited papers | No link to a practical BCI question |
| Data audit and neurophysiology | 15% | Complete provenance; expected ERP or ERD shown before decoding | Missing units or events; no signal check |
| Preprocessing and quality control | 15% | Every choice justified with evidence; rejection counts reported | Defaults with no justification |
| Decoding and evaluation | 20% | Leakage-free pipeline, grouped CV, chance level, per-subject results | Random epoch split, or tuning on test data |
| Hypothesis test and interpretation | 15% | Controlled comparison with variability and a statistical test; limits stated honestly | Claims unsupported by the numbers |
| Reproducibility and code quality | 5% | Runs top to bottom on fresh Colab; seeds and versions pinned | Fails to run |
| Presentation and Q&A | 10% | Clear 12-minute story; every member answers questions on any stage | One member presents everything |
| Optional extension | +5% | Out-of-scope method compared fairly against the in-scope baseline | — |

